R"FREL(<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Versions &amp; deployments | FortisNet Node</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/fortis-favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><style>
:root{color-scheme:dark;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;background:#05090d;color:#edf8fb;--cyan:#22e1ff;--muted:#aac0ca;--line:#28434f}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0}a{color:var(--cyan);text-underline-offset:4px}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--cyan);outline-offset:4px}header{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);padding:22px max(22px,5vw);display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between}header nav{display:flex;gap:24px;font-size:14px}main{max-width:1250px;margin:auto;padding:42px 24px 70px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,48px);font-weight:550;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:0 0 12px}h2{font-size:23px;font-weight:500;margin:0 0 15px}p{margin:0 0 18px}.intro,.muted{color:var(--muted)}.intro{max-width:850px}.eyebrow{font:14px monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--cyan);margin-bottom:15px}.notice{padding:15px 18px;border:1px solid #497585;background:#10242d;margin:24px 0;font-size:14px}.notice.error{border-color:#b06567;background:#311e25}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.25fr 1fr;gap:22px}.panel{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:24px;background:#0b171e;margin-bottom:24px;min-width:0}.state{color:var(--cyan);font:14px monospace;margin-bottom:18px}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:155px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px 18px;font-size:14px}dt{color:var(--muted)}dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}code{font:14px/1.65 monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.hash{padding:13px;background:#050d12;border:1px solid var(--line);display:block;margin:12px 0}button{font:14px system-ui;background:#132d38;color:#edf8fb;border:1px solid #547988;padding:10px 14px;cursor:pointer}button:hover{background:#1c414f}button:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:14px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap}td.time{min-width:225px}td small{display:block;font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}td code{white-space:nowrap}details{margin-top:30px}summary{cursor:pointer}details p{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:16px}.paging{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:20px}.paging span,.foot{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}[hidden]{display:none!important}@media(max-width:800px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:30px 18px 50px}.panel{padding:20px}dl{grid-template-columns:125px minmax(0,1fr);gap:10px}.scroll{margin:0 -5px}header{padding:20px}header nav{gap:18px}}@media(max-width:370px){dl{grid-template-columns:1fr}dd{margin-bottom:8px}}
</style></head><body><header><a href="/">FortisNet / Node</a><nav aria-label="Node navigation"><a href="/dashboard">Live dashboard</a><a href="/errors">Errors</a></nav></header><main><p class="eyebrow">OPEN INFRASTRUCTURE / RELEASE TRANSPARENCY</p><h1>Versions &amp; deployments.</h1><p class="intro">See the exact executable this node is running, how a new version is progressing, and the periods when each deployment was observed serving traffic.</p><div id="notice" class="notice" role="status">Loading controller observations. Missing information is shown as unknown.</div><noscript><p class="notice">Live release observations need JavaScript. Read the public JSON at <a href="/releasesz">/releasesz</a>. History is available at <a href="/releasesz/history?page=0">/releasesz/history?page=0</a>; the current feed names the latest page.</p></noscript><div class="grid"><section class="panel" aria-labelledby="current-title"><h2 id="current-title">Running now</h2><p id="state" class="state">Waiting for identity</p><dl id="current"></dl><code id="hash" class="hash">Executable SHA-256 unavailable</code><button id="copy" type="button" disabled>Copy full SHA-256</button></section><section class="panel" aria-labelledby="candidate-title"><h2 id="candidate-title">Update progress</h2><p id="candidate-state" class="state">Waiting for controller</p><dl id="candidate"></dl><p class="foot">An uploaded package is not automatically executed. The controller verifies its signature, runs an isolated preflight, drains the old worker, checks storage and observes the candidate before accepting it.</p></section></div><section class="panel" aria-labelledby="history-title"><h2 id="history-title">Serving history</h2><p class="muted">Each activation is a separate row. A rollback or restart can run the same executable again. All displayed times are UTC.</p><div class="scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable deployment history"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Deployment</th><th scope="col">Release / executable</th><th scope="col">Serving observations (UTC)</th><th scope="col">Outcome / reason</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history"><tr><td colspan="4">No deployment observations loaded.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="paging"><button id="older" type="button" disabled>Older</button><button id="newer" type="button" disabled>Newer</button><button id="latest" type="button">Latest</button><span id="page"></span></div></section><details><summary>How to interpret hashes, times and rollback</summary><p>The version is a human-readable label. The full SHA-256 identifies the executable bytes verified by the controller. Source commit is separate signed build provenance and can be unknown for earlier releases. Signature verification describes admission; it does not prove that all services or providers are healthy.</p><p>Serving boundaries are first-confirmed controller observations, not exact first/last request times. Process startup, readiness, disabling new traffic and finishing accepted work are different events. Unknown or uncertain boundaries remain labelled. The release running before this ledger was installed has no invented historical start.</p><p>The current embedded database has one owning process. Updates include a controlled handover interruption. Rollback recovers compatible code using the latest durable data; it does not erase acknowledged writes or reverse actions already performed by external services.</p><p>Missing traffic is insufficient evidence to accept a candidate. Node faults and third-party failures are assessed separately: for example, an exhausted CoinGecko quota is not by itself proof of a broken release. This page refreshes observations; if the controller or connection stops, its last values may be stale.</p></details><p class="foot">Public records exclude credentials, wallet contents, device identities and internal host paths. <a href="/releasesz">Current JSON</a> · <a id="raw-history" href="/releasesz/history?page=0">History JSON</a> · <a id="design-link" href="https://github.com/FortisNet/node">Source &amp; documentation</a></p></main><script>
(()=>{'use strict';const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);let digest='',page=null,latest=0,previous=null,busy=false,followLatest=true;const value=v=>v===null||v===undefined?'Unknown':String(v);const time=v=>{if(!Number.isSafeInteger(v)||v<=0)return'Unknown';const d=new Date(v);return Number.isNaN(d.getTime())?'Unknown':d.toISOString().replace('T',' ').replace('Z',' UTC')};function fields(id,entries){const list=$(id);list.replaceChildren();for(const [key,text]of entries){const dt=document.createElement('dt'),dd=document.createElement('dd');dt.textContent=key;dd.textContent=value(text);list.append(dt,dd)}}function notice(text,error=false){$('notice').textContent=text;$('notice').classList.toggle('error',error)}async function json(url){const response=await fetch(url,{cache:'no-store'});if(!response.ok)throw Error('Release observations unavailable (HTTP '+response.status+').');const data=await response.json();if(data.schemaVersion!==1)throw Error('Release observations have an unsupported format.');return data}async function history(target){const data=await json('/releasesz/history?page='+target);if(!Array.isArray(data.records)||data.records.length>25||data.page!==target)throw Error('Invalid history page.');page=target;previous=data.previousPage;$('history').replaceChildren();for(const r of data.records){const row=document.createElement('tr');for(const text of ['D'+value(r.deploymentId)+' / instance '+value(r.instanceId),value(r.version)+'\n'+value(r.sha256).slice(0,16)+'…',time(r.trafficEnabledAtMs)+' → '+(r.trafficDisabledAtMs?time(r.trafficDisabledAtMs):(r.stoppedAtMs||r.outcome==='crashed'?'End unknown':'No confirmed end')),value(r.outcome)+' / '+value(r.reason)]){const cell=document.createElement('td');cell.textContent=text;row.append(cell)}row.children[2].className='time';const note=document.createElement('small');note.textContent=r.timeUncertain?'Observed or uncertain boundaries; original start may be unknown.':'Confirmed controller observations.';row.children[2].append(note);$('history').append(row)}if(!data.records.length){const row=document.createElement('tr'),cell=document.createElement('td');cell.colSpan=4;cell.textContent='No deployments recorded on this page.';row.append(cell);$('history').append(row)}$('older').disabled=previous===null;$('newer').disabled=page>=latest;$('page').textContent='Page '+(page+1);$('raw-history').href='/releasesz/history?page='+page}async function refresh(){if(busy)return;busy=true;try{const data=await json('/releasesz');if(data.managed===false){notice('This runtime has no controller release metadata. Version hashes and deployment history are unknown.');$('state').textContent='Unmanaged / metadata not installed';$('candidate-state').textContent='No controller observations';fields('current',[]);fields('candidate',[]);digest='';$('hash').textContent='Executable SHA-256 unknown';$('copy').disabled=true;return}const age=Date.now()-data.observedAtMs;if(!Number.isFinite(age)||age< -5000)notice('Controller clock differs from this device; freshness cannot be established.',true);else if(age>15000)notice('Controller observation is stale. Last confirmed: '+time(data.observedAtMs)+'.',true);else notice('Controller observed this state at '+time(data.observedAtMs)+'. Serving boundaries are first-confirmed observations.');const r=data.current;if(r&&/^(?:[a-f0-9]{40}|[a-f0-9]{64})$/.test(r.sourceCommit||'')){$('design-link').href='https://github.com/FortisNet/node/blob/'+r.sourceCommit+'/docs/node-updates.md';$('design-link').textContent='Update design'}$('state').textContent=r?value(r.phase)+' · '+value(r.version):'No worker currently confirmed serving';fields('current',r?[['Deployment','D'+r.deploymentId],['Instance',r.instanceId],['Source commit',r.sourceCommit],['Process started',time(r.processStartedAtMs)],['Serving confirmed',time(r.trafficEnabledAtMs)],['Stable confirmed',time(r.stableAtMs)],['Signature',r.signatureVerified===true?'Verified at admission':'Not verified']]:[]);digest=r&&/^[a-f0-9]{64}$/.test(r.sha256)?r.sha256:'';$('hash').textContent=digest||'Executable SHA-256 unknown';$('copy').disabled=!digest;const c=data.candidate;$('candidate-state').textContent=c?value(c.phase)+' · '+value(c.version):'No candidate awaiting promotion';fields('candidate',c?[['Deployment','D'+c.deploymentId],['Requested',time(c.requestedAtMs)],['Last transition',time(c.updatedAtMs)],['Outcome',c.outcome],['Reason',c.reason]]:[]);latest=data.latestPage;if(!Number.isSafeInteger(latest)||latest<0)throw Error('Invalid history cursor.');if(followLatest||page===null)await history(latest)}catch(error){notice(error.message+' Last known values remain visible and may be stale.',true)}finally{busy=false}}$('copy').addEventListener('click',async()=>{try{await navigator.clipboard.writeText(digest);$('copy').textContent='SHA-256 copied'}catch{$('copy').textContent='Select the SHA-256 above to copy'}});async function go(target){try{await history(target)}catch(error){notice(error.message,true)}}$('older').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(previous!==null){followLatest=false;void go(previous)}});$('newer').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(page<latest){followLatest=false;void go(page+1)}});$('latest').addEventListener('click',()=>{followLatest=true;void go(latest)});void refresh();setInterval(refresh,5000)})();
</script></body></html>)FREL"
